{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":294224,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9fc8e8b9-6dca-4255-bf7f-239417c0480a","total_cost_usd":1.3239180000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":66070,"cache_read_input_tokens":20672,"output_tokens":24160,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":66070,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":24160,"cache_read_input_tokens":20672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":66070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":66070},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":48777,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.048872,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":24160,"cacheReadInputTokens":20672,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66070,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2750460000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"spec-auditor\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n  \"summary\": \"Sixteen of eighteen checks hold, but the full-hold parachute descent breaks the 5 m/s soft-landing rule once the catalog's own masses are used (5.06 m/s, not the asserted 4.60), and that failure exists because the full-hold mass the params assert (806 kg) is 30% lighter than the mass the catalog actually produces (1149.9 kg).\",\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"band_names_consistent\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"statement\": \"Every band name used in the catalog or the params appears in the baseline's bands, and no band is referenced that the baseline does not define.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Baseline defines {suborbital, low, high}. Catalog uses exactly those three across all 24 debris entries and all 3 band_summary entries. Params reference bands in ablation.heat_index, ablation.cost_curve, ablation.optimal_skims and economy.band_value_multiplier — each is exactly {suborbital, low, high}. No fourth name appears anywhere; Mr. Armstrong's satellite is correctly absent from both the catalog and the band keys.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"debris-designer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"band_summary_matches_debris\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"statement\": \"Every band_summary entry agrees with the debris array it summarises: piece_count, mean_mass_kg and fragile_fraction all recomputed.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Suborbital: 8 pieces, (140+380+460+60+110+95+70+1150)/8 = 2465/8 = 308.125 kg, fragile spawn weight (5+4)/87 = 0.1034 — claimed 8 / 308.125 / 0.103. Low: 8 pieces, 5090/8 = 636.25 kg, (5+4+3)/67 = 0.1791 — claimed 8 / 636.25 / 0.179. High: 8 pieces, 8720/8 = 1090.0 kg, (6+4+3+1)/56 = 0.2500 — claimed 8 / 1090 / 0.25. All three match, and fragile_fraction is correctly spawn-weighted rather than counted (by count it would read 0.25 / 0.375 / 0.50).\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"debris-designer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"mean_mass_rises_by_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"statement\": \"The catalog's mean piece mass rises band over band, so valuable junk physically fights you.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"308.125 -> 636.25 -> 1090.0 kg, i.e. 2.07x then 1.71x, 3.54x end to end. Excluding the crane-only oversized piece in each band the trend holds and steepens: 187.9 -> 441.4 -> 831.4 kg (4.43x). Mass per crushed slot, which is what actually reaches the physics, rises the same way: 134.4 -> 247.5 -> 403.9 kg/slot.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"debris-designer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"fragile_share_rises_by_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"statement\": \"Fragile spawn share rises across the bands, roughly 1 in 10 suborbital to 1 in 4 high.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Spawn-weighted fragile share: suborbital 9/87 = 0.103 (1 in 9.7), low 12/67 = 0.179 (1 in 5.6), high 14/56 = 0.250 (1 in 4.0). Monotone rising and both endpoints land on the GDD's stated 1-in-10 and 1-in-4.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"debris-designer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"full_hold_doubles_mass\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.5\",\n      \"statement\": \"A full hold roughly doubles the rocket's mass at starting storage size.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Spawn-weighted over all hand-tetherable suborbital and low pieces (fragiles charged their uncrushed slot cost, since compactor t1 never crushes them): mass 15855+29950 = 45805 kg against slots 118+121 = 239, i.e. 191.65 kg per crushed slot. 6 base slots = 1149.9 kg against dry_mass_kg 850, so loaded/dry = 1999.9/850 = 2.35x. That is 17.6% above doubling, inside the 25% tolerance, but at the heavy end — and it is not the 1.95x the params' own balance note claims (that note used 806 kg, a suborbital-only hold).\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"ablation_optimum_shape\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"statement\": \"The cheapest descent is 1 to 2 skims from the high band, no band's optimum exceeds the high band's, each minimum matches optimal_skims, and the curve is what the stated model produces.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Minima: suborbital [9.13, 9.67, 11.57, 15.58] at k=0; low [18.83, 18.03, 19.10, 22.71] at k=1; high [40.16, 36.43, 35.67, 38.41] at k=2 — high's optimum is in {1,2}, and 0 <= 1 <= 2 so the return leg gets harder with altitude. optimal_skims {0, 1, 2} matches all three minima. Model recomputed as 0.53*sum(1.9^i, i=0..k) + 0.00029*(heat_index*skim_mult[k])^2.4 + k*0.00029*26^2.4, skim unit 0.00029*2488.5 = 0.7217: suborbital k=0 = 8.597+0.53 = 9.127 (array 9.13), k=1 = 7.411+1.537+0.722 = 9.670 (9.67); low k=0 = 18.298+0.53 = 18.828 (18.83), k=1 = 15.773+1.537+0.722 = 18.031 (18.03); high k=0 = 39.640+0.53 = 40.170 (40.16), k=2 = 30.780+3.450+1.443 = 35.674 (35.67), k=3 = 29.161+7.086+2.165 = 38.412 (38.41). Largest deviation 0.03%. NOTE: this passes on the curve as the charter directs; the flown results measure the optimum at 1 pass in all nine band-and-load cases with ablation monotone increasing, which is reported in observations.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"skim_multiplier_matches_measured\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"statement\": \"The claimed skim_heat_multiplier matches what was flown, compared entry by entry for the high band, within 0.10 at every index.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Claimed [1, 0.94, 0.90, 0.88] against measured high-band skim_heat_multiplier_measured [1, 0.96, 0.92, 0.882] at fixed entry_depth 0: deltas 0.000, 0.020, 0.020, 0.002 — all well inside 0.10, and the guess is conservative in the right direction (it claims slightly more cooling than flown). Caveat for the human, not a failure of this check: the same array is 0.198 out at index 1 for the suborbital band (measured [1, 0.742, 0.742, 0.742]) and the measured effect also moves with entry depth (suborbital one-skim ratio 0.742 / 0.807 / 0.922 at depths 0 / 19500 / 39000 m), so a single global array cannot represent the quantity even though it happens to be accurate where it was checked.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"skim_curve_and_toll_growth_shape\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"statement\": \"skim_heat_multiplier starts at 1.0, is non-increasing and flattens by its last two entries; cycle_toll_growth exceeds 1.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"[1, 0.94, 0.90, 0.88]: first entry exactly 1.0; strictly non-increasing; successive drops 0.060, 0.040, 0.020, so the last step is half the previous and a third of the first — the benefit saturates rather than continuing to fall. cycle_toll_growth = 1.9 > 1, giving per-cycle tolls 0.53 / 1.01 / 1.91 / 3.64% and cumulative 0.53 / 1.54 / 3.45 / 7.09%, which is what makes the compounding toll outrun the shrinking heat saving (high band skim 3 saves only 0.00029*(106138-100557) = 1.62% against a 3.64% fourth-cycle toll).\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"parachute_full_hold_soft_landing\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.2\",\n      \"statement\": \"Parachute descent speed at full hold is under the 5 m/s soft-landing threshold, and above about 3.5 m/s so the Parachute upgrade is a real purchase.\",\n      \"result\": \"fail\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Using the params' own stated model, v = sqrt(2mg/(rho*Cd*A)) with rho*Cd*A = 626 at g = 4.0: the asserted descent_speed_full_hold_ms = 4.6 reproduces only at m = 1656 kg (sqrt(13248/626) = 4.60), which is 850 dry + a 806 kg hold. The catalog's own spawn weights put a 6-slot hold at 1149.9 kg (191.65 kg/crushed slot), so m = 1999.9 kg and v = sqrt(15999.2/626) = sqrt(25.558) = 5.06 m/s — over the line, a hard landing at the starting band with no cargo upgrades bought, and double damage on every fragile piece aboard. The simulator's independent figure is 4.99 m/s, soft by 0.01 m/s, but it is not independent: the params carry no canopy area, so the simulator back-solved 357.1 m2 from the 4.60 m/s claim itself. Either way there is no margin, and the upper bound (>3.5 m/s) is not the problem.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"Raise parachute_drag_coefficient (and add the canopy area to the params so the claim is checkable) until a 1999.9 kg full hold lands with real margin under 5 m/s, then restate descent_speed_full_hold_ms as what that model produces rather than as an input.\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"tow_fee_clamps\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.3\",\n      \"statement\": \"The tow fee is zero inside the free radius, linear beyond it, clamps at exactly 50%, and can never go negative or exceed the cap.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"free_radius_m = 2000, max_fee_fraction = 0.5, curve = linear. Half circumference = pi*250000 = 785398 m. fee(d) = 0.5*(d-2000)/(785398-2000) clamped to [0, 0.5]: fee(0..2000) = 0; fee(2000) = 0 exactly; fee(393699) = 0.2500; fee(785398) = 0.5000 exactly at the antipode; the clamp's lower bound forbids negatives and the upper bound forbids exceeding half. Charged against haul value only, so payout runs 100% at the pad down to 50% at the far side and never touches savings.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"lazy_run_breaks_even\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.6\",\n      \"statement\": \"Launch cost is at or below the value of three cheap suborbital pieces.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Cheapest suborbital piece = size_class_base_value.small 40 x band_value_multiplier.suborbital 1.0 = 40. Three of them = 120. launch_cost = 100 <= 120, i.e. 2.5 cheap smalls, matching the GDD's '2-3 pieces of cheap junk'. A six-slot hold of the cheapest thing in the band grosses 240 and clears 140 against launch alone.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"steady_tow_never_shears\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.4\",\n      \"statement\": \"Steady-state towing never shears a magnet: per-cable tension at the heaviest legal two-piece load stays below magnet_hold_force_n with margin.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Heaviest legal two-piece hand-tethered load in the catalog is iridium_battery_stack 1150 kg + dense_avionics_core 1000 kg = 2150 kg. a = jetpack_thrust_n / (suit_mass + towed) = 500/(120+2150) = 0.2203 m/s2, so the worst cable carries 1150 x 0.2203 = 253.3 N against magnet_hold_force_n = 900 — a 3.55x margin. Inside the shipping slice the worst pair is satellite_bus_frame 700 + propellant_tank_shell 620: a = 500/1440 = 0.3472, tension 243 N, 3.70x margin. The general bound holds too: T_i = m_i*F/(m_suit + sum m) < F = 500 N < 900 N for any legal load, so steady thrust can never reach the hold force and shear can only fire on the impulsive latch and swing terms.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"staging_is_one_way\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"statement\": \"No parameter anywhere reintroduces thrust after staging.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"thrust_n 12000, rcs_thrust_n 600, fuel_burn_kgs 3.2 and rcs_fuel_burn_kgs 0.16 all belong to the jettisoned stage; no params field grants post-stage propulsion, and none of the twelve upgrades touches one (they move fuel_capacity_kg, thrust_n, base_slots, heat_capacity, parachute_drag_coefficient and magnet_hold_force_n only). The sole post-stage impulse is eva.jetpack_thrust_n = 500 N on the hull: at a loaded staged 1999.9 kg that is 0.25 m/s2, and the whole 24 kg of EVA propellant at 0.7 kg/s gives 34.3 s x 500 N = 17143 N.s = 8.6 m/s of orbit change — a rescue, not an engine.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"fragile_never_crushed_and_premium\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.4\",\n      \"statement\": \"Fragile is never crushable at any compactor tier present in the params, and the fragile premium makes one intact fragile piece worth several solid pieces of the same class and band.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"cargo.compactor_tier = 1 is the only tier present — no compactor entry appears in the upgrades list — and t1 crushes small solids only. Nothing in the params overrides the catalog's per-piece fragile flag or grants crushing by class, so no fragile piece is crushable at any tier that exists. fragile_value_premium = 3: a suborbital fragile small is 40 x 1.0 x 3 = 120 against 40 for a solid small, exactly three solid pieces of the same class and band; a low-band fragile medium is 90 x 2.4 x 3 = 648 against 216. Per slot the premium is thinner because fragiles pay uncrushed cost — 120 over 2 slots = 60/slot against 40/slot solid, i.e. 1.5x — which is noted for the human rather than failed here.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"oversized_rejects_hand_magnet\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.4\",\n      \"statement\": \"Oversized junk rejects the hand magnet — hand_tetherable is false for that class.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"size_classes.oversized.hand_tetherable = false, against true for small and medium. All three oversized pieces (derelict_upper_stage 1150 kg, tumbling_comsat_core 2000 kg, mirrored_survey_array 2900 kg) therefore accept only the crane cable, and they carry slot costs 6 crushed / 12 uncrushed against a 6-slot base hold, so none of them can ride home at starting storage in any case.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"debris-designer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"twelve_upgrade_purchases\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.6\",\n      \"statement\": \"Twelve upgrade purchases: six parts, two tiers each, tier 2 dearer than tier 1, each tier improving the stat it names.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"12 entries, 6 parts x 2 tiers: fuel_tank 400/1200, thruster 350/1000, storage 500/1500, heat_shield 450/1300, parachute 420/1200, hand_magnet 380/1100 — tier 2 dearer in every case. Stats improve monotonically from base: fuel_capacity_kg 450->620->850, thrust_n 12000->15000->19000, base_slots 6->9->12, heat_capacity 100->130->165, parachute_drag_coefficient 1.8->2.6->3.6 (higher Cd = slower descent = better), magnet_hold_force_n 900->1400->2100. Matches the slice's stated six-part, two-tier, twelve-purchase shop.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"slice_bands_populated\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.1\",\n      \"statement\": \"Both shipping-slice bands are populated with at least one fragile piece and at least two size classes, so the player meets crushing and meets fragility inside the slice.\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Suborbital: 2 fragile pieces (cracked_camera_dome 95 kg, battered_antenna_whip 70 kg) and 3 size classes (5 small, 2 medium, 1 oversized). Low: 3 fragile pieces (cracked_solar_array, parabolic_dish_section, star_tracker_head) and 3 size classes (3 small, 4 medium, 1 oversized). Both bands give the player crushable smalls for compactor t1 and an uncrushable fragile to meet the exception. Reported for the human: literal flight reachability is a separate matter — the measured results show all three ascents failing with fuel_remaining_kg = 0, so no band is currently reachable as parameterised.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"\",\n      \"owner\": \"debris-designer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"rule_id\": \"no_target_moved\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"statement\": \"No rule passes only because a quantity the design states as fixed, or a quantity being measured, was moved to meet it.\",\n      \"result\": \"fail\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The GDD's stated constants all survived: cargo.base_slots = 6 (2.2 'Cargo reads 4 of 6'), eva.base_tether_slots = 2 (appendix), landing.soft_landing_ms = 5, no_gear_multiplier = 2, fragile_multiplier = 2, tow_fee.max_fee_fraction = 0.5, magnet_range_screens = 0.125 (1/8 screen), cargo_damage_interval_s = 3, heat_dissipation_s = 5, compactor_tier = 1. What moved instead is the measured quantity itself, in three places. (1) The full-hold mass: the params reason from 806 kg (134.4 kg/slot, suborbital only) while the catalog's own spawn weights over the shipping slice give 191.65 kg/slot and 1149.9 kg — 43% heavier. Both the 'roughly doubles' claim (1.95x asserted, 2.35x actual) and the 4.60 m/s descent speed are computed against the lighter figure, and the soft-landing rule fails once the real one is used. (2) landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms is carried as an input with no canopy area beside it, so the outcome being audited is asserted rather than derived — the simulator had to back-solve 357.1 m2 from that very number, making its 4.99 m/s confirmation circular by construction. (3) dry_mass_kg = 850 against the 1400 kg staged mass the baseline's ballistic-coefficient derivation assumed: flown beta is 161.9 kg/m2, 39% below the 267 kg/m2 on which the whole multi-pass aerobraking argument — and therefore the skim economy the cost_curve prices — was built.\",\n      \"fix_hint\": \"Re-derive from the catalog rather than from assumption: take 191.65 kg per crushed slot and a 1149.9 kg full hold as the input, add landing.parachute_area_m2 and the staged structural mass to the schema so descent speed and beta are computable from the file, and let descent_speed_full_hold_ms and heat_index fall out of the model instead of being stated.\",\n      \"owner\": \"economy-balancer\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observations\": [\n    \"The flown data says the ablation optimum is one pass everywhere. cheapest_pass_count = 1 in all nine band-and-load cases and ablation is monotone increasing in pass count — high band full hold runs 19.6, 28.6, 30.5, 31.5 ... 40.1 at 20 passes. The authored cost_curve is internally faithful to its own coefficients (I recomputed eight points to within 0.03%), so this is not an arithmetic error in the params; it is that the model's skim benefit is priced per-band from a global array while the flown benefit saturates after one skim at the starting band. The 2-4 pass optimum is the design's third pillar and it does not exist as flown. This is the most important thing on the page for a human.\",\n    \"Every full-hold descent exceeds the heat gate on its own cheapest trajectory: peak heat 112 / 106 / 102 against heat_capacity = 100. That means a full hold from the starting band with the starting shield begins damaging cargo, one slot every 3 s. The GDD wants heat capacity to gate the top of the progression, not the opening loop. No listed check covers this, so it is here rather than in checks.\",\n    \"The full-hold touchdown lands at 4.99 m/s against a 5.00 m/s grading line. Even if the parachute is retuned, a landing grade decided by 0.01 m/s is a coin flip the player cannot feel or influence; the soft/hard boundary wants either visible margin or a graded band rather than a cliff.\",\n    \"A fragile medium is uncrushable and costs 4 of the 6 base slots, so two of them fill the starting hold. In the low band — the slice's second band and where fragile mediums live — the fragile detour is therefore all-or-nothing rather than the 'sometimes clearly worth it, sometimes clearly not' the GDD asks for. The params' author flagged this too and priced around it rather than moving base_slots, which was the right call.\",\n    \"Multi-skim descents cost hours of in-world time: the measured three-skim descents run 3.38-4.09 h against orbital periods of 44-80 minutes. Time compression is not an optimisation here, it is the difference between a playable descent and an unplayable one, and it is currently on the deferred list.\",\n    \"EVA at load may read as unresponsive rather than heavy. jetpack_fuel_kg 24 at 0.7 kg/s is 34 s of continuous burn; with two low-band mediums in tow (1320 kg) acceleration is 0.35 m/s2 and total delta-v is 11.9 m/s, which is roughly 37 s to cross 200 m and stop. The fix if it plays badly is the catalog's mass column, not jetpack_thrust_n — raising thrust enough to fix the loaded case makes the empty astronaut twitchy.\",\n    \"The lazy-run margin is thinner than the launch cost alone suggests. launch_cost 100 clears the three-cheap-pieces bar at 120, but a suborbital descent at the authored optimum burns 9.13% of plate and replate_cost_per_pct = 3 adds 27, so real fixed cost is 127 — just over the bar. At the flown ablation (8.5% empty, 24.4% full hold) a greedy suborbital run pays 73 in replating alone.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":194696,"ttft_stream_ms":7378,"time_to_request_ms":250,"type":"result","duration_ms":292485,"uuid":"af538042-850c-477e-8372-98c0aca0b30d"}
